<article class="env-lemma" id="0GRC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GRC">Lemma <span data-tag="0GRC">103.17.8</span>.</a> In the situation discussed above, the equivalence $\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}) \cong \mathit{QCoh}(U, R, s, t, c)$ sends coherent sheaves to coherent sheaves and vice versa, i.e., induces an equivalence $\textit{Coh}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}) \cong \textit{Coh}(U, R, s, t, c)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is immediate from the definition of coherent $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X}$-modules. For bookkeeping purposes: the material above uses Morphisms of Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/06R6" data-tag="06R6">101.17.5</a>, Algebraic Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/04T4" data-tag="04T4">94.16.1</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/04WY" data-tag="04WY">94.16.3</a>, Sheaves on Stacks, Section <a href="/tag/06WU" data-tag="06WU">96.15</a>, Sheaves on Stacks, Proposition <a href="/tag/06WT" data-tag="06WT">96.14.3</a>, and Groupoids in Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/0GPN" data-tag="0GPN">78.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>